discobsd-host (1.0.8) noble; urgency=medium

  * discobsd-web: a viewer whose socket is reset (a tab closed with data
    unread, which macOS reports as ECONNRESET) ends the session quietly
    instead of printing a traceback for every such disconnect.
  * README: a macOS section; the console needs no driver there, the node
    is /dev/cu.usbmodemrp20401, and pipx from Homebrew is the install.

 -- DiscoBSD RP2040 port <noreply@github.com>  Tue, 16 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0000

discobsd-host (1.0.7) noble; urgency=medium

  * discobsd-web: a viewer that goes silent is pinged and, if it does not
    answer, dropped after two intervals (30 s), so a page kept alive by
    the browser's cache or a device that left the LAN no longer holds the
    one console forever; the page closes its socket on pagehide and
    reloads when restored from the cache; client pings get pongs.

 -- Oichkatzelesfrettschen <discobsd-pico@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 08:00:00 -0700

discobsd-host (1.0.6) noble; urgency=medium

  * ports: match the board on Windows, where the PnP manager reports the
    USB serial number upper-cased ("RP2040") and usbser.sys exposes no
    product string; discobsd-term --list and the web console found no
    board there since 1.0.0.

